import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 695 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 696 | 2026-10-27 | **Grade 5 Workbooks: Scales and Arpeggios, Keys and Intervals, Chords and Cadences (Build BD).** One page per Lesson Book step, as the Grade 4 Workbooks: TRY IT (the first one worked as the example), YOUR TURN (a week of ticks) and PLAY (a few quick answers), then On paper, the check-up (four parts, four marks each, pass 3+). Scales: finger 4 in each of the four-octave keys; which way (p, f, < >, staccato); mirror twins or not; both hands' chromatic fingers from B and C♯/D♭; arpeggio fingers. Keys: name the key (up to seven sharps or flats, both clefs); the melodic minor going up (sharp, double sharp, natural); augmented and diminished intervals; inversions; where the tune goes (dominant, subdominant, relative) with the note that tells. Chords: name the first inversion (vii°b too); I, Ib or Ic before V-I; passing or auxiliary; the chord before V; harmonise eight notes. The three teacher's copies gain the TRY IT and PLAY answers and the check-up scoring (the Chords and Cadences copy is now three pages). Found while checking: the Chords and Cadences step 3 page and check-up overflowed in print; tightened. Source patch723.py; test ax717.js (scales-5, keys-5, harmony-5: no overflow). |",
"| 697 | 2026-10-27 | **Grade 5 lessons in three existing rooms (Build BE; board call 23).** Melody: A melody for a four-line stanza (Theory Grade 5): three stanzas (two in 2/4, one of them with an anacrusis, and one in 3/4), any key up to three sharps or flats, major or minor; a note for every syllable with the words under the notes; checked: starts on 1, 3 or 5, mostly by step, lines 1-3 end away from the tonic, line 4 on it, a phrase mark over each line; an example melody for each. Form: Four forms from the great composers: minuet and trio, scherzo, air with variations (a theme, a quaver variation and a minor variation played), recitative and aria, each drawn as letters with one example to listen to, and a which-form question. Stories (Pitch and range): The woodwinds: flute, oboe, clarinet in B♭ and in A, bassoon, each range lit on the whole keyboard (sounding), the clef it reads and how it transposes; a which-instrument question from the range and clef. Ranges, transpositions and the form examples are from general knowledge and flagged on the board for her to check. Home: the three lessons sit on the Grade 5 floor. Source patch724.py; test be724.js. chsweep 46 chapters 0 errors, booksweep 0 errors, regression 322 lessons, 54 drills, 0 errors. Local commit only, not pushed. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
